<title>USA: NO DAMAGING COLD SEEN IN BRAZIL COFFEE AREAS- WSC.</title>
<headline>NO DAMAGING COLD SEEN IN BRAZIL COFFEE AREAS- WSC.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>No damaging cold is in sight for Brazil's coffee growing areas during the next five days, independent forecaster Weather Services Corp (WSC) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The forecast is for dry weather Tuesday and Wednesday, with low temperatures of 50-65 degrees F. Thursday to Saturday will be dry and mild, WSC said.</p>
